Apple today released new firmware for the AirPods Pro 2, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-pro/">AirPods Pro 3</a>, AirPods 4, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods/">AirPods 5</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-max/">AirPods Max 2</a>. The firmware has a build number of 9B47, up from 9A348/9A350.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/airpods-5-new-blue.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066076" /><br/>
Apple has been <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/airpods-beta-firmware-9b5045a/">beta testing the new firmware</a> for the last several weeks, but hasn't yet offered details on what's included in the software. Apple has <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/106340">an AirPods support document</a> that it will update with information soon.<br/>
<br/>
